      "topic": "Common Factor Method",
      "marks": 2,
      "id": "lba_qa_1"
    },
    {
      "q": "Factorise x^2 + 5x + 6.",
      "a": "Find two numbers that multiply to 6 and add to 5: they are 2 and 3.\nSplit the middle term:\nx^2 + 2x + 3x + 6\n= x(x + 2) + 3(x + 2)\n= (x + 2)(x + 3)\n\nSo x^2 + 5x + 6 = (x + 2)(x + 3). ✅",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "topic": "Splitting the Middle Term",
      "marks": 3,
      "id": "lba_qa_2"
    },
    {
      "q": "Factorise the expression 4a^2 - 9 using an identity.",
      "a": "This is a difference of squares: a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b).\n4a^2 = (2a)^2 and 9 = 3^2.\n\n4a^2 - 9 = (2a)^2 - 3^2\n= (2a + 3)(2a - 3)\n\nSo 4a^2 - 9 = (2a + 3)(2a - 3). ✅",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "topic": "Difference of Squares",
      "marks": 3,
      "id": "lba_qa_3"
    },
